hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15738","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sayyar and Yahya ibn Sa'id the judge, that they heard Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah narrating from his father. As for Sayyar, he said: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and as for Yahya, he said: from his father, from his grandfather, he said: We pledged the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hearing and obedience in our hardship and our ease, and our activity and our dislike, and preference over us, and not to dispute authority with its people, and to stand with the truth wherever it be, and not to fear in Allah the blame of any blamer."
"15739","He said: And Shu'bah said: Sayyar did not mention this phrase, and wherever it be, Yahya mentioned it. Shu'bah said: If I mentioned anything in it, it is from Sayyar or from Yahya."
